cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or these results, please cite the article below. THIS
  RECORD IS NOT YET COMPLETE: every value beginning '[AUTHOR NOTE' is a
  placeholder the authors must replace, so this file does not yet identify a
  citable article (6 outstanding: article_authors, article_doi,
  article_title, article_year, repository_code, software_authors).
title: "PREDIX HER2 — multimodal prediction of pathological complete response"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, deposited cross-validation artefacts and a verification
  notebook for the multimodal (clinical, transcriptomic, genomic, proteomic and
  whole-slide-image) prediction of pathological complete response in the
  PREDIX HER2 randomised trial. This is the no-patient-data variant of the
  deposit: the trial's individual-level input matrix is not included, pending
  the decision on releasing individual-level data. What individual-level
  information the deposited cross-validation artefacts still carry is set out
  in docs/NO_PATIENT_DATA.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "[AUTHOR NOTE: add the author list, in the article's order]"
    given-names: ""
repository-code: "[AUTHOR NOTE: add the GitHub URL after the first push]"
# MIT applies to the SOFTWARE ONLY. CITATION.cff has one licence field and no
# way to express that, so the scope notice in LICENSE governs — see it before
# reusing anything under results/ or report/.
license: "MIT"
version: "2.0.0-revision1+nodata"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
keywords:
  - breast cancer
  - HER2
  - multimodal machine learning
  - pathological complete response
  - cross-validation
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "[AUTHOR NOTE: article title]"
  journal: "Nature Cancer"
  # Quoted on purpose. Unquoted, the bracket would make this a YAML sequence
  # rather than a placeholder, and the file would not parse as a citation record.
  year: "[AUTHOR NOTE: year]"
  doi: "[AUTHOR NOTE: DOI once assigned]"
  authors:
    - family-names: "[AUTHOR NOTE: add the article's author list]"
      given-names: ""
